# Git and deployment

- Never force-push. Do not rewrite established history unless explicitly asked.
- Make logical commits. Do not push unless asked.
- The public site is `https://siam.rice.edu/`. `astro.config.mjs` `site` and `public/CNAME` stay on that name. `https://rice-siam.github.io/` redirects there.
- This is the organization-root Pages repository. Do not set an Astro `base` path.
- Deploy through GitHub Actions (`withastro/action` + `deploy-pages`).
- Before creating a commit, run `npm run lint`, `npm run format:check`, `npm run test:schedule`, `npm run build`, and `npm run test:a11y`. All five must pass. If one fails, fix it and re-run that check. Do not commit on a failure.
- The same five checks must pass before push.
- The deploy workflow rebuilds nightly so dated events move from upcoming to past without client-side JavaScript.
